        <div
          x-data="{ id: $id('accordion') }"
          :class="{ 'text-white': activeAccordion==id, 'text-slate-300 hover:text-accent-500': activeAccordion!=id }"
          class="cursor-pointer group text-slate-300 hover:text-accent-500"
        >
          <button
            type="button"
            @click="setActiveAccordion(id)"
            :id="`${id}-trigger`"
            :aria-expanded="activeAccordion == id"
            :aria-controls="`${id}-panel`"
            class="flex items-center justify-between w-full p-4 pb-1 text-left font-medium select-none"
          >
            <span>Why record Open Gate with OpenCam?</span>
            <svg
              style="min-width: 20px; min-height: 20px; width: 20px; height: 20px;"
              class="duration-300 ease-out text-accent-500 flex-shrink-0 !shrink-0"
              :class="{ '-rotate-[45deg]': activeAccordion==id }"
              xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
              fill="none"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              stroke-width="1.5"
              stroke="currentColor"
              ><path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                d="M12 6v12m6-6H6"></path></svg
            >
          </button>
          <div
            :id="`${id}-panel`"
            role="region"
            :aria-labelledby="`${id}-trigger`"
            x-show="activeAccordion==id"
            x-collapse=""
          >
            <div class="p-4 pt-2 text-slate-300">
              OpenCam records in a true 4:3 aspect ratio using your iPhone’s full sensor — capturing more of the scene without cropping or distortion.
              <br>
On iPhone 17 and iPhone Air, experience the new 1:1 full-sensor square mode, perfect for creators who shoot for both portrait and landscape formats.
<br>
With Apple Log and Open Gate recording, you’ll preserve every stop of dynamic range for precise color grading, complete with real-time LUT previews to see your look as you film.
              <br>
              <br>
              You can now just film a single video, and have more room to edit it for both vertical and horizontal formats, for platforms like YouTube, TikTok, Instagram, and more.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
