        <div
          x-data="{ id: $id('accordion') }"
          :class="{ 'text-white': activeAccordion==id, 'text-slate-300 hover:text-accent-500': activeAccordion!=id }"
          class="cursor-pointer group text-slate-300 hover:text-accent-500"
        >
          <button
            type="button"
            @click="setActiveAccordion(id)"
            :id="`${id}-trigger`"
            :aria-expanded="activeAccordion == id"
            :aria-controls="`${id}-panel`"
            class="flex items-center justify-between w-full p-4 pb-1 text-left font-medium select-none"
          >
            <span
              >Does OpenCam have a teleprompter?</span
            >
            <svg
              style="min-width: 20px; min-height: 20px; width: 20px; height: 20px;"
              class="duration-300 ease-out text-accent-500 flex-shrink-0 !shrink-0"
              :class="{ '-rotate-[45deg]': activeAccordion==id }"
              xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
              fill="none"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              stroke-width="1.5"
              stroke="currentColor"
              ><path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                d="M12 6v12m6-6H6"></path></svg
            >
          </button>
          <div
            :id="`${id}-panel`"
            role="region"
            :aria-labelledby="`${id}-trigger`"
            x-show="activeAccordion==id"
            x-collapse=""
            style="display: none;"
          >
            <div class="p-4 pt-2 text-slate-300">
              Yes. Paste your script and it appears over the camera preview while you record, so you can read to camera without extra gear. It can scroll at a steady pace, or follow your voice using on-device speech recognition on iOS 26 and later, which works offline once your language is downloaded. You can change the text size, width and position, and the script is never recorded into your video.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div
          x-data="{ id: $id('accordion') }"
          :class="{ 'text-white': activeAccordion==id, 'text-slate-300 hover:text-accent-500': activeAccordion!=id }"
          class="cursor-pointer group text-slate-300 hover:text-accent-500"
        >
          <button
            type="button"
            @click="setActiveAccordion(id)"
            :id="`${id}-trigger`"
            :aria-expanded="activeAccordion == id"
            :aria-controls="`${id}-panel`"
            class="flex items-center justify-between w-full p-4 pb-1 text-left font-medium select-none"
          >
            <span
              >How is my data handled?</span
            >
            <svg
              style="min-width: 20px; min-height: 20px; width: 20px; height: 20px;"
              class="duration-300 ease-out text-accent-500 flex-shrink-0 !shrink-0"
              :class="{ '-rotate-[45deg]': activeAccordion==id }"
              xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
              fill="none"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              stroke-width="1.5"
              stroke="currentColor"
              ><path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                d="M12 6v12m6-6H6"></path></svg
            >
